.TH NETDOC 1 "2026-08-09" "network-doctor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netdoc \- diagnose network connectivity and explain where the connection breaks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netdoc
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netdoc
diagnoses network connectivity layer by layer and reports where the path
breaks in plain English. With no
.I target
it runs the generic local and internet checks; with a
.I target
it also probes that endpoint.
.PP
Probes run unprivileged and time-bounded, and form a dependency graph with
independent branches, so an unrelated failure never hides a working path.
.PP
By default
.B netdoc
starts a terminal UI. With
.B \-json
it runs headless and prints a machine-readable report instead.
.PP
Flags may be given before or after the
.IR target ,
and each accepts both the single-dash and double-dash spelling
.RB ( \-json
and
.BR \-\-json
are the same flag).
.SH TARGET
.TP
.B example.com
hostname (default port 443)
.TP
.B example.com:8022
hostname with port (protocol inferred from the port)
.TP
.B ssh://example.com:8022
URL (scheme sets protocol and default port; path ignored)
.TP
.BR 192.0.2.1 ", " 2001:db8::1
IP literal
.TP
.B [2001:db8::1]:443
IP literal with port (IPv6 needs the brackets)
.PP
Recognized URL schemes are
.BR http ,
.BR https ,
.BR ssh ,
and
.BR smtp .
At most one target may be given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-toolbox
Start in toolbox mode, which opens directly on the network tools pane
.RB ( ping ,
.BR dig ,
.BR curl ,
.BR traceroute ,
.BR mtr ,
.BR ss ,
.BR ip ,
.BR nmap )
instead of the diagnosis view. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-json .
.TP
.B \-json
Run the checks headless and print a JSON report on standard output. The field
names and the status vocabulary
.RB ( PASS ,
.BR WARN ,
.BR FAIL ,
.BR SKIP ,
.BR N/A )
are a stable contract, safe to script against.
.TP
.B \-watch
Continuously re-run the checks, starting another pass five seconds after each
one finishes. In the terminal UI this shows the last 20 states and a failure
count per check. Combined with
.BR \-json ,
it streams one compact JSON report per line until the process is interrupted;
those lines carry an extra
.B ts
field (RFC 3339, UTC) and are otherwise the one-shot report unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-iface " name\fR|\fPaddress"
Bind probe traffic to an interface name or to an exact local IP address, so
the checks follow a specific link (a VPN tunnel, a second NIC) rather than the
system's default route.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " duration"
Per-check probe timeout, as a Go duration string such as
.B 2s
or
.BR 1500ms .
Must be positive. The default is
.BR 4s .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-h
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The chain completed with no failed row. Skipped rows are allowed.
.TP
.B 1
A row failed, the terminal UI was quit before the chain finished, or the run
itself errored. Under
.B \-json \-watch
this is the last completed pass's status.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments, or a target the parser rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run the generic local and internet diagnosis:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose the path to a host, over HTTP, TLS, and HTTPS:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc github.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Let the port select the protocol rows, here the SSH banner check:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc github.com:22
.EE
.RE
.PP
Keep SSH on a nonstandard port with an explicit scheme:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc ssh://host:2222
.EE
.RE
.PP
Get one JSON report on standard output, for scripts, CI, or a bug report:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc \-\-json github.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Follow an intermittent failure as it happens:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc \-\-json \-\-watch github.com | jq \-c 'select(.ok | not) | {ts, failed_stage, summary}'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Send the probes out through a specific interface:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc \-\-iface wg0 github.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use the exit status in a shell script:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
netdoc github.com || echo "path to github is broken"
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/netdoc/history
Up to 50 recent targets, saved by the terminal UI between sessions. Normally
.IR ~/.config/netdoc/history .
On macOS this is
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/netdoc/history ,
and on Windows
.IR %AppData%\enetdoc\ehistory .
Exit
.B netdoc
and delete the file to clear the history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR dig (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR traceroute (8),
.BR mtr (8),
.BR ss (8),
.BR ip (8),
.BR nmap (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.PP
Full documentation, including the JSON report schema and the verdict table:
.UR https://github.com/heymaikol/network-doctor
.UE
